<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Aer Lingus cabin crew dispute settled - radio.</title>
<headline>Irish Aer Lingus cabin crew dispute settled - radio.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strike threatened by cabin crews of Irish airline, Aer Lingus, over their New York hotel accommodation appears to have been settled, RTE radio said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Aer Lingus said the strike, which was due to begin at midnight, was called off after lenghty discussions at Ireland's Labour court.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the airline said it had been agreed that the crews would continue to stay at the two hotels they currently use and there would be further discussions on outstanding issues of security and room service, RTE radio said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
